  "articleBody": "Facing a misdemeanor charge can be daunting, and it's easy to make mistakes that could impact your case. Knowing what pitfalls to steer clear of can significantly improve your chances of a favorable outcome. Here are some common missteps and how to avoid them:\n\n*   **Talking to the Police Without Counsel:** This is probably the biggest one. You might think you can talk your way out of it, but anything you say can be used against you. Don't waive your right to remain silent. Instead, politely state that you wish to speak with your attorney before answering any questions.\n*   **Ignoring the Charges:** Hoping it will just ",
